---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { email } from '../config';
---

<DocLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  h1="Stillroom Vault refund policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="Stillroom Vault refunds: a full refund within 14 days of purchase, no questions asked, handled by Paddle, our Merchant of Record."
  lead="14 days, no questions asked."
  updated="29 October 2026"
  legal
>
    <h2 id="how">Within 14 days, for any reason</h2>
    <p>
      If Stillroom Vault isn’t right for you, ask for a refund within 14 days of buying and you’ll get your money back in
      full. You don’t have to give a reason. This applies to every edition: a Family or Teams order is refunded as a whole.
      It comes on top of your legal rights as a consumer, never instead of them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ask">How to ask</h2>
    <p>Either way works:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Reply to your Paddle receipt, or use the order help link in it.</li>
      <li>
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${email.support}`}>{email.support}</a> from the address you bought with, and we’ll pass it
        on.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our
      orders. Paddle provides all customer service inquiries and handles returns. Refunds go back to the way you paid; how
      long that takes depends on your bank or card.
    </p>

    <h2 id="after">What happens after a refund</h2>
    <p>
      Please stop using the licence key: Stillroom checks keys offline, so it can’t know about a refund, and we trust you.
      Your vault isn’t touched either way. Without a key Stillroom is the free tier (up to 25 items, every feature), and
      opening, exporting and backing up always keep working.
    </p>

    <h2 id="later">After 14 days</h2>
    <p>
      Write to us anyway if something’s wrong. If Stillroom doesn’t work as described, we’ll make it right, and your rights
      as a consumer under the law of your country always apply.
    </p>

    <h2 id="free">Try it first</h2>
    <p>
      The free tier has every feature, so you can use Stillroom with real files before you pay. Exporting everything is
      always possible, licensed or not.
    </p>
</DocLayout>
